    <briefdescription>
<para>RAII wrapper for FILE* handles. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Automatically closes the file on destruction. Supports move semantics to enable use in containers and return values.</para>
<para>Exception-safe: destructor is noexcept and safely handles null pointers.</para>
<para>Example: <programlisting><codeline><highlight class="normal">{</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><ref refid="classthemis_1_1llm_1_1_scoped_file_1afd8a537a4169fe6133fb03bc6b36f6a2" kindref="member">ScopedFile</ref><sp/>f(fopen(</highlight><highlight class="stringliteral">&quot;data.bin&quot;</highlight><highlight class="normal">,<sp/></highlight><highlight class="stringliteral">&quot;rb&quot;</highlight><highlight class="normal">));</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/></highlight><highlight class="keywordflow">if</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/>(!f)<sp/>{</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/></highlight><highlight class="keywordflow">throw</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/>std::runtime_error(</highlight><highlight class="stringliteral">&quot;Failed<sp/>to<sp/>open<sp/>file&quot;</highlight><highlight class="normal">);</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>}</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/></highlight><highlight class="comment">//<sp/>Use<sp/>f.get()<sp/>to<sp/>access<sp/>FILE*</highlight><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">}<sp/><sp/></highlight><highlight class="comment">//<sp/>fclose()<sp/>automatically<sp/>called<sp/>here</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting> </para>
    </detaileddescription>
